module

public import StacksFrontier.Homology.QuasiIsoColimit
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.CechIndexCategory
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.PresentedCechDatum

/-!
# Stacks 099D, step 2: the datum carried across the filtered colimit

Step 2 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099D] passes from the presented pairs — the objects of
`Stacks.PairSite.Pair` — to an arbitrary pair `(A, I)` with `I` finitely generated, by the
filtered colimit over the index category `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver A I` constructed in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/CechIndexCategory.lean`. This file carries the three pieces of
data and the two strict conditions of the tag across that colimit, and reduces the whole of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData` to the two conditions that live in a derived
category.

The engine is the universal property of the colimit written in terms of the germ maps
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ`: `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.descGerm` descends a compatible
family of semilinear maps out of the values of a pair-module, and
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.hom_ext_germAt` says that a map out of the colimit is determined by
what it does to germs. Every identity below is proved by evaluating both sides on a germ.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germAt` — `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ`, read as a function into
  the colimit module itself instead of into its restriction of scalars along the structure map.
  Every statement below is phrased with it: the two targets are definitionally equal, but not
  syntactically, and `rw` fails on the unreduced spelling.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.descGerm` — the map out of the colimit determined by a compatible
  family of germs, with `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.descGerm_germAt` the defining formula.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureHom` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureIso` — the identification `colim 𝒪 ≅ A`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap` — datum (3) of the tag at the colimit, on a single
  pair-module: the semilinear comparison induced by `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap`,
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureSingleIso` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitAugmentation` — the same on complexes, and datum (2).
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.self` and `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitSelfIso` — the index
  category of a *presented* pair has a terminal object, so the colimit at a presented pair is
  the value of the pair-module there.
* `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitBaseChange` and `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitCechIso` — conditions (c) and
  (d) of the tag for the colimit complex, as propositions. These are the two statements this
  file does *not* prove in general; it proves them at the presented pairs.

## Main results

* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitFunctor_structureModule` — **`colim 𝒪 ≅ A`**: the colimit of
  the structure presheaf of pairs is `A`, read in `ModuleCat A`. The germ formula is
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureHom_germAt`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap_comp` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_comp` — **condition (b) at the colimit, on the
  nose**: the comparison maps compose with no derived-category comparison intervening. The
  strictness is inherited from `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport_comp`, which is `rfl`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap_structureModule` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_augmentation` — **condition (a) at the colimit, on
  the nose**.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitSelfNatIso` — the colimit functor of a presented pair is
  evaluation at that pair.
* `Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData_of_presented` — **the assembly**: a
  `Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum` whose colimit complex satisfies conditions (c) and (d)
  gives a `Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData`. Fields (1), (2), (3), (a) and (b) are
  discharged here.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.hasExactColimitsOfShape` — **AB5 at the shape of the index
  category**, and `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isStableUnderColimitsOfShape_quasiIso` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.quasiIso_of_isColimit` — **a colimit of quasi-isomorphisms over the
  index category is a quasi-isomorphism**. These are the two homological inputs the transport of
  conditions (c) and (d) across the colimit needs.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_lift_span` — an object of the index category whose
  ideal is generated by **lifts of a prescribed** finite generating family of `I`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_left` and
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_right` — the base-change comparison of
  condition (c) is the adjoint of its argument, so it is natural in it. In particular an
  isomorphism of either complex changes the comparison only by an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap_self`,
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_self` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitAugmentation_self` — **the colimit datum at a presented pair
  is the datum of `Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum`**: the comparison maps of datum (3) and
  the augmentation of datum (2) correspond under
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexSelfIso`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.isIso_derivedBaseChange_colimitComplexMap_self` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.exists_cech_iso_colimit_self` — **conditions (c) and (d) for the colimit
  complex hold at the presented pairs**, respectively at the morphisms of presented pairs. They
  are the transports of the datum's own two fields.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks 099D]` attribute is attached: this file produces an unconditional term of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData` only once it is fed a term of
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum` (step 3). That term is
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_presentedCechDatum`, and it does *not* follow the source's own argument
for step 3, which `Stacks.PairSite.exists_injective_not_injective_value` refutes; it is the
filtered colimit of the Čech complexes over the generating families instead. The attribute sits
on the assembled term, `Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_functorialCechData`.

The two propositions `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitBaseChange` and `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitCechIso`
are hypotheses of `Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData_of_presented` only because this
file does not prove them: they are conditions in a derived category at an *arbitrary* pair,
whereas the colimit complex is identified with the datum's own complex only at the presented
pairs, where `Stacks.PairSite.isIso_derivedBaseChange_colimitComplexMap_self` and
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_cech_iso_colimit_self` prove them directly. Both are now theorems for
every `Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum`, with no further hypothesis:
`Stacks.PairSite.colimitBaseChange` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/CechGermBaseChangeProof.lean` and
`Stacks.PairSite.colimitCechIso` in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/CechColimitCechIso.lean`, whose
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData` joins them.

Both rest on one statement, for a chosen `X : Stacks.PairSite.PairOver A I`:

`IsIso (Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange X.hom w)`, where `w` is the degreewise germ
map `Stacks.PairSite.sectionsComplex Dat.complex X.pair ⟶
(CochainComplex.restrictScalars X.hom).obj ((colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex)`.

That is `Stacks.PairSite.GermBaseChange`, proved by `Stacks.PairSite.germBaseChange`; the proof
is the filtered-colimit argument: a K-flat replacement `P ⟶ Dat.complex(X.pair)`, the datum's
(c) at every morphism out of `X`, the cofinality
`CategoryTheory.Under.final_forget`, and
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.quasiIso_of_isColimit`. Granted it, condition (d) follows by choosing
`X` with `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_lift_span`, applying the datum's own (d) at
`X.pair` and the Čech base change
`Stacks.CechRingBaseChange.isIso_derivedBaseChange_extendedComplexMap`; and condition (c)
follows from the same statement at `(A, I)` and at `(B, J)` together with the transitivity law
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp`. Note that "`DerivedCategory.Q` preserves
colimits of shape `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver A I`" is *not* among the inputs, and is false for a
general filtered shape: for a sequence `K₀ → K₁ → ⋯` the group
`Hom_{D(A)}(colim Kₙ, Z)` differs from `lim Hom_{D(A)}(Kₙ, Z)` by a `lim¹` term.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

/-! ### Base change along a ring map, and composition -/

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]

open CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars

/-- **Pre-composing the comparison of condition (c) with a map of complexes.** The base-change
comparison `Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange` is the adjoint of its argument, so
pre-composition with `a : K' ⟶ K` becomes composition with the image of `a` under derived
extension of scalars. This is the naturality of the adjunction in its left variable, spelled with
`Functor.mapHomologicalComplex`; `Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_left` is the
same statement spelled with `CochainComplex.restrictScalars`, which is the spelling the
conditions of [Stacks, Tag 099D] use and in which `rw` succeeds. -/
theorem derivedBaseChange_comp_left' (φ : A →+* B) {K K' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
    {L : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ} (a : K' ⟶ K)
    (u : K ⟶ ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapHomologicalComplex
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj L) :
    derivedBaseChange φ (a ≫ u) =
      (derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} φ).functor.map (DerivedCategory.Q.map a) ≫
        derivedBaseChange φ u := by
  have h : DerivedCategory.Q.map (a ≫ u) ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.inv.app L =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map a ≫ (DerivedCategory.Q.map u ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.inv.app L) := by
    rw [Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  exact (congrArg _ h).trans (Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left_symm _ _ _)

/-- **Post-composing the comparison of condition (c) with a map of complexes of `B`-modules.**
The `Functor.mapHomologicalComplex` spelling; see
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_right`. -/
theorem derivedBaseChange_comp_right' (φ : A →+* B) {K : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
    {L L' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ}
    (u : K ⟶ ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapHomologicalComplex
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj L) (v : L ⟶ L') :
    derivedBaseChange φ (u ≫ ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map v) =
      derivedBaseChange φ u ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map v := by
  have h : DerivedCategory.Q.map (u ≫ ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map v) ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.inv.app L' =
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map u ≫
          (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.inv.app L) ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategory.map (DerivedCategory.Q.map v) := by
    have hn := (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} φ).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.inv.naturality v
    simp only [Functor.comp_map] at hn
    rw [Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, hn, ← Category.assoc]
  exact (congrArg _ h).trans (Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right_symm _ _ _)

/-- **Pre-composing the comparison of condition (c) with a map of complexes of `A`-modules.** If
`a` is a quasi-isomorphism this says that `IsIso (derivedBaseChange φ u)` may be tested after
replacing `K` by any complex quasi-isomorphic to it, which is how a K-flat replacement enters. -/
theorem derivedBaseChange_comp_left (φ : A →+* B) {K K' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
    {L : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ} (a : K' ⟶ K)
    (u : K ⟶ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj L) :
    derivedBaseChange φ (a ≫ u) =
      (derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} φ).functor.map (DerivedCategory.Q.map a) ≫
        derivedBaseChange φ u :=
  derivedBaseChange_comp_left' φ a u

/-- **Post-composing the comparison of condition (c) with a map of complexes of `B`-modules.**
In particular an isomorphism of the target complex changes the comparison only by an
isomorphism, which is what transports condition (c) along an identification of `K(B, J)`. -/
theorem derivedBaseChange_comp_right (φ : A →+* B) {K : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
    {L L' : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ}
    (u : K ⟶ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj L) (v : L ⟶ L') :
    derivedBaseChange φ (u ≫ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map v) =
      derivedBaseChange φ u ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map v :=
  derivedBaseChange_comp_right' φ u v

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

namespace Stacks.PairSite

variable {A B D : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing D]
variable {I : Ideal A} {J : Ideal B} {L : Ideal D}

namespace PairOver

/-! ### The universal property of the colimit, in terms of germs -/

/-- The presheaf of modules on the index site obtained from a pair-module by pulling back along
the projection `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.proj`. This is the object whose colimit
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitFunctor` takes. -/
abbrev indexModule (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    PresheafOfModules.{u} (indexRings A I) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀.{u} (proj A I).op structureRings.{u}).obj M

/-- **The germ map, read as a function into the colimit module itself.** This is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ` with its target `(ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj (colim M)`
replaced by the definitionally equal `colim M`. The two spellings are not syntactically equal,
and `rw` refuses to rewrite under the first one, so every statement below uses this one. -/
def germAt (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver A I) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).obj M :=
  germ hI M X m

/-- `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germAt` is `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ`. -/
theorem germAt_eq (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver A I) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    germAt hI M X m = germ hI M X m := rfl

/-- **The cocone condition for the germ maps**, in the spelling of
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germAt`. -/
theorem germAt_restriction (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (m : M.value X.pair) :
    germAt hI M Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = germAt hI M X m :=
  germ_restriction hI M f m

/-- The germ map is semilinear along the structure map of the object. -/
theorem germAt_smul (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver A I) (r : X.pair.ring)
    (m : M.value X.pair) :
    germAt hI M X (r • m) = X.hom r • germAt hI M X m :=
  (germ hI M X).hom.map_smul r m

/-- A compatible family of semilinear maps out of the values of a pair-module, read as a
morphism of presheaves of modules into the constant presheaf. This is the datum the adjunction
`PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction` consumes; its naturality is exactly the compatibility of
the family with the restriction maps. -/
def coconeHom (M : PairModule.{u}) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (g : ∀ X : PairOver A I, M.value X.pair ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj N)
    (hg : ∀ {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) (m : M.value X.pair),
      g Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = g X m) :
    (indexModule A I M) ⟶ (PresheafOfModules.constFunctor (indexRingCocone A I)).obj N :=
  { app := fun Z => g Z.unop.unop
    naturality := fun {_ _} f =>
      ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun m => hg f.unop.unop m) }

/-- **The universal property of the colimit.** A family of maps `M(X.pair) ⟶ N` of
`X.pair.ring`-modules, compatible with the restriction maps of the pair-module, descends to an
`A`-linear map out of the colimit. -/
def descGerm (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (g : ∀ X : PairOver A I, M.value X.pair ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj N)
    (hg : ∀ {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) (m : M.value X.pair),
      g Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = g X m) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).obj M ⟶ N :=
  haveI := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  haveI := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  (PresheafOfModules.ModuleColimit.homEquiv (isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)
    (colimit.isColimit (indexModule A I M).presheaf)).symm (coconeHom M N g hg)

/-- The defining formula for `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.descGerm`: it takes the germ at `X` to
the value of the given family at `X`. -/
theorem descGerm_germAt (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (g : ∀ X : PairOver A I, M.value X.pair ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj N)
    (hg : ∀ {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) (m : M.value X.pair),
      g Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = g X m)
    (X : PairOver A I) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    descGerm hI M N g hg (germAt hI M X m) = g X m := by
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  have := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  exact PresheafOfModules.ModuleColimit.homEquiv_symm_apply _ _ (coconeHom M N g hg)
    (X := op (op X)) m

/-- **Every element of the colimit is a germ.** -/
theorem germAt_jointly_surjective (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u})
    (m : (colimitFunctor hI).obj M) :
    ∃ (X : PairOver A I) (x : M.value X.pair), germAt hI M X x = m := by
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  have := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  obtain ⟨U, x, hx⟩ := PresheafOfModules.ModuleColimit.ιM_jointly_surjective
    (hcR := isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)
    (hcM := colimit.isColimit (indexModule A I M).presheaf) m
  exact ⟨U.unop.unop, x, hx⟩

/-- **A map out of the colimit is determined by what it does to germs.** This is the
extensionality principle every identity below is proved with. -/
theorem hom_ext_germAt (hI : I.FG) {M : PairModule.{u}} {N : ModuleCat.{u} A}
    {h h' : (colimitFunctor hI).obj M ⟶ N}
    (H : ∀ (X : PairOver A I) (m : M.value X.pair),
      h (germAt hI M X m) = h' (germAt hI M X m)) :
    h = h' := by
  refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun m => ?_)
  obtain ⟨X, x, rfl⟩ := germAt_jointly_surjective hI M m
  exact H X x

/-- The germ maps are natural in the pair-module. -/
theorem germAt_naturality (hI : I.FG) {M N : PairModule.{u}} (α : M ⟶ N) (X : PairOver A I)
    (m : M.value X.pair) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).map α (germAt hI M X m) =
      germAt hI N X (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app α X.pair.ix m) := by
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  have := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  exact PresheafOfModules.ModuleColimit.map_apply _ _ _
    ((PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀.{u} (proj A I).op structureRings.{u}).map α)
    (U := op (op X)) m

/-! ### The colimit of the structure presheaf is `A` -/

/-- The structure map of an object of the index category, read as a map of modules out of the
value of the structure presheaf. -/
def structureGerm (X : PairOver A I) :
    structureModule.{u}.value X.pair ⟶
      (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj (ModuleCat.of A A) :=
  ConcreteCategory.ofHom (C := ModuleCat.{u} X.pair.ring)
    { toFun := X.hom
      map_add' := X.hom.map_add
      map_smul' := fun a x => X.hom.map_mul a x }

/-- The structure maps form a cocone: this is `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.hom_apply_toRingHom`. -/
theorem structureGerm_restriction {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (m : structureModule.{u}.value X.pair) :
    structureGerm Y (structureModule.{u}.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = structureGerm X m :=
  hom_apply_toRingHom f m

/-- **The comparison map `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A`**, induced by the structure maps. -/
def colimitStructureHom (hI : I.FG) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).obj structureModule.{u} ⟶ ModuleCat.of A A :=
  descGerm hI structureModule.{u} (ModuleCat.of A A) structureGerm
    (fun {_ _} f m => structureGerm_restriction f m)

/-- **The formula for `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A` on germs**: the germ of `r ∈ A₀` goes to its image in `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitStructureHom_germAt (hI : I.FG) (X : PairOver A I) (r : X.pair.ring) :
    colimitStructureHom hI (germAt hI structureModule.{u} X r) = X.hom r :=
  descGerm_germAt hI structureModule.{u} (ModuleCat.of A A) structureGerm
    (fun {_ _} f m => structureGerm_restriction f m) X r

/-- A chosen object of the index category; it exists because `I` is finitely generated. -/
def base (hI : I.FG) : PairOver A I := (nonempty (I := I) hI).some

/-- The germ of `1` at the chosen object. It generates `colim 𝒪` as an `A`-module. -/
def oneGerm (hI : I.FG) : (colimitFunctor hI).obj structureModule.{u} :=
  germAt hI structureModule.{u} (base hI) (1 : (base hI).pair.ring)

/-- The germs of `1` at any two objects of the index category agree, because a morphism of
pairs preserves `1`. -/
theorem germAt_structureModule_one (hI : I.FG) {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    germAt hI structureModule.{u} Y (1 : Y.pair.ring) =
      germAt hI structureModule.{u} X (1 : X.pair.ring) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (germAt_restriction hI structureModule.{u} f (1 : X.pair.ring))
  exact congrArg (germAt hI structureModule.{u} Y) ((Hom.toHom f).toRingHom.map_one).symm

/-- The germ of `r` of the structure presheaf at `X` is `X.hom r` times the germ of `1` at `X`. -/
theorem germAt_structureModule_smul (hI : I.FG) (X : PairOver A I) (r : X.pair.ring) :
    germAt hI structureModule.{u} X r =
      X.hom r • germAt hI structureModule.{u} X (1 : X.pair.ring) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (germAt_smul hI structureModule.{u} X r (1 : X.pair.ring))
  exact congrArg (germAt hI structureModule.{u} X) (mul_one r).symm

/-- **`colim 𝒪` is generated by `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.oneGerm`**: every germ of the
structure presheaf is a multiple of it. Filteredness is what lets the two objects be compared. -/
theorem germAt_structureModule_eq_smul (hI : I.FG) (X : PairOver A I) (r : X.pair.ring) :
    germAt hI structureModule.{u} X r = X.hom r • oneGerm hI := by
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  have h : germAt hI structureModule.{u} X (1 : X.pair.ring) = oneGerm hI :=
    (germAt_structureModule_one hI (IsFiltered.leftToMax X (base hI))).symm.trans
      (germAt_structureModule_one hI (IsFiltered.rightToMax X (base hI)))
  rw [germAt_structureModule_smul hI X r, h]

/-- The map `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A` sends `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.oneGerm` to `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitStructureHom_oneGerm (hI : I.FG) :
    colimitStructureHom hI (oneGerm hI) = 1 :=
  (colimitStructureHom_germAt hI (base hI) 1).trans (base hI).hom.map_one

/-- The map `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A` sends `a • oneGerm hI` to `a`. -/
theorem colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm (hI : I.FG) (a : A) :
    colimitStructureHom hI (a • oneGerm hI) = a := by
  rw [(colimitStructureHom hI).hom.map_smul, colimitStructureHom_oneGerm, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

/-- Every element `m` of `colim 𝒪` is its image under `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A` times
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.oneGerm`. -/
theorem eq_colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm (hI : I.FG)
    (m : (colimitFunctor hI).obj structureModule.{u}) :
    m = colimitStructureHom hI m • oneGerm hI := by
  obtain ⟨X, x, hx⟩ := germAt_jointly_surjective hI structureModule.{u} m
  have e : m = X.hom x • oneGerm hI := hx.symm.trans (germAt_structureModule_eq_smul hI X x)
  have h2 : colimitStructureHom hI m = X.hom x := by
    rw [e, colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm]
  rw [h2]
  exact e

/-- The map `colim 𝒪 ⟶ A` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_colimitStructureHom (hI : I.FG) : IsIso (colimitStructureHom hI) := by
  rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
  refine ⟨fun m m' h => ?_, fun a => ⟨a • oneGerm hI, colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm hI a⟩⟩
  rw [eq_colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm hI m, eq_colimitStructureHom_smul_oneGerm hI m', h]

/-- **`colim 𝒪 ≅ A`.** The colimit, over the index category of Stacks 099D's step 2, of the
structure presheaf of pairs is `A` itself, read in `ModuleCat A`. This is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isColimit_indexRingCocone` read on modules rather than on rings, and
it is what makes the augmentation of the tag descend to the colimit. The formula on germs is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureHom_germAt`. -/
def colimitStructureIso (hI : I.FG) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).obj structureModule.{u} ≅ ModuleCat.of A A :=
  asIso (colimitStructureHom hI)

/-- The forward map of `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureIso` is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureHom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitStructureIso_hom (hI : I.FG) :
    (colimitStructureIso hI).hom = colimitStructureHom hI := rfl

/-- **`colim 𝒪 ≅ A`**, in the existential form. -/
theorem colimitFunctor_structureModule (hI : I.FG) :
    Nonempty ((colimitFunctor (A := A) (I := I) hI).obj structureModule.{u} ≅
      ModuleCat.of A A) :=
  ⟨colimitStructureIso hI⟩

/-! ### Datum (3) at the colimit -/

/-- **Datum (3) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit**, on a single pair-module: the semilinear
comparison `colim_{(A,I)} M ⟶ colim_{(B,J)} M` induced by a ring map `φ : A →+* B` with
`J = IB`. It is the descent of the family of germs at the transported objects
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport`, which is possible because
`((transport φ hφ).obj X).hom = φ.comp X.hom` on the nose. -/
def colimitMap (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).obj M ⟶
      (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj ((colimitFunctor hJ).obj M) :=
  descGerm hI M ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj ((colimitFunctor hJ).obj M))
    (fun X => germ hJ M ((transport φ hφ).obj X))
    (fun {_ _} f m => germ_restriction hJ M ((transport φ hφ).map f) m)

/-- The comparison map of datum (3) takes a germ to the germ at the transported object. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitMap_germAt (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver A I) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ M (germAt hI M X m) = germAt hJ M ((transport φ hφ).obj X) m :=
  descGerm_germAt hI M ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).obj ((colimitFunctor hJ).obj M))
    (fun X => germ hJ M ((transport φ hφ).obj X))
    (fun {_ _} f m => germ_restriction hJ M ((transport φ hφ).map f) m) X m

/-- The comparison map of datum (3) is natural in the pair-module. This is what makes it a map
of *complexes* in `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap`. -/
theorem colimitMap_naturality (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    {M N : PairModule.{u}} (α : M ⟶ N) :
    (colimitFunctor hI).map α ≫ colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ N =
      colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ M ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).map ((colimitFunctor hJ).map α) := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt hI fun X m => ?_
  rw [ModuleCat.comp_apply, ModuleCat.comp_apply, germAt_naturality,
    ModuleCat.restrictScalars.map_apply, colimitMap_germAt, colimitMap_germAt]
  exact (germAt_naturality hJ α ((transport φ hφ).obj X) m).symm

/-- **Condition (b) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit, on the nose**, in a single degree: the
comparison maps of datum (3) compose, with no comparison in a derived category intervening. The
strictness is inherited from `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport_comp`, which holds by `rfl`. -/
theorem colimitMap_comp (φ : A →+* B) (ψ : B →+* D) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hL : L.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) (hψ : L = Ideal.map ψ J) (hχ : L = Ideal.map (ψ.comp φ) I)
    (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    colimitMap (ψ.comp φ) hI hL hχ M =
      colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ M ≫ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).map (colimitMap ψ hJ hL hψ M) ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalarsComp φ ψ).inv.app ((colimitFunctor hL).obj M) := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt hI fun X m => ?_
  change colimitMap (ψ.comp φ) hI hL hχ M (germAt hI M X m) =
    colimitMap ψ hJ hL hψ M (colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ M (germAt hI M X m))
  rw [colimitMap_germAt, colimitMap_germAt]
  exact (colimitMap_germAt ψ hJ hL hψ M ((transport φ hφ).obj X) m).symm

/-- **Condition (a) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit, on the nose**, in a single degree: the
comparison map of datum (3) is compatible with the identification `colim 𝒪 ≅ A`. -/
theorem colimitMap_structureModule (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) :
    colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ structureModule.{u} ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).map (colimitStructureHom hJ) =
      colimitStructureHom hI ≫ LocalCohomology.restrictedRingHom φ := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt hI fun X r => ?_
  change colimitStructureHom hJ (colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ structureModule.{u}
      (germAt hI structureModule.{u} X r)) =
    φ (colimitStructureHom hI (germAt hI structureModule.{u} X r))
  rw [colimitMap_germAt, colimitStructureHom_germAt hI X r]
  exact colimitStructureHom_germAt hJ ((transport φ hφ).obj X) r

/-! ### The index category of a presented pair has a terminal object -/

/-- **The object of the index category of a presented pair given by the identity.** It is the
terminal object (`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isTerminalSelf`), so the colimit of step 2 at a
presented pair is the value of the pair-module there. -/
def self (P : Pair.{u}) : PairOver P.ring P.ideal where
  pair := P
  hom := RingHom.id P.ring
  map_ideal := Ideal.map_id P.ideal

/-- The unique morphism to `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.self`: its underlying ring map is forced to
be the structure map, and the condition on ideals is then the object's own. -/
def toSelf {P : Pair.{u}} (X : PairOver P.ring P.ideal) : X ⟶ self P :=
  ⟨⟨X.hom, X.map_ideal.symm⟩, RingHom.id_comp X.hom⟩

/-- Every morphism to `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.self` is `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.toSelf`. -/
theorem toSelf_unique {P : Pair.{u}} {X : PairOver P.ring P.ideal} (f : X ⟶ self P) :
    f = toSelf X :=
  Hom.ext' (Pair.Hom.ext' ((RingHom.id_comp (Hom.toHom f).toRingHom).symm.trans (Hom.w f)))

/-- **The index category of a presented pair has a terminal object**, namely the pair itself
with the identity. -/
def isTerminalSelf (P : Pair.{u}) : IsTerminal (self P) :=
  IsTerminal.ofUniqueHom toSelf fun _ f => toSelf_unique f

/-- The restriction map to the terminal object. -/
def selfHom (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver P.ring P.ideal) :
    M.value X.pair ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj (M.value P) :=
  M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf X))

/-- The restriction maps to the terminal object form a cocone. -/
theorem selfHom_restriction (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u})
    {X Y : PairOver P.ring P.ideal} (f : X ⟶ Y) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    selfHom P M Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = selfHom P M X m := by
  have h : Hom.toHom f ≫ Hom.toHom (toSelf Y) = Hom.toHom (toSelf X) :=
    congrArg Hom.toHom (toSelf_unique (f ≫ toSelf Y))
  change M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf Y)) (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) =
    M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) m
  rw [← PairModule.restriction_comp_apply M (Hom.toHom f) (Hom.toHom (toSelf Y)) m, h]

/-- The comparison map from the colimit at a presented pair to the value there. -/
def colimitSelfHom (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    (colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg).obj M ⟶ M.value P :=
  descGerm P.ideal_fg M (M.value P) (selfHom P M)
    (fun {_ _} f m => selfHom_restriction P M f m)

/-- The comparison map from the colimit at a presented pair sends the germ of `m` at `X` to the
restriction of `m` to the terminal object. -/
theorem colimitSelfHom_germAt (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u})
    (X : PairOver P.ring P.ideal) (m : M.value X.pair) :
    colimitSelfHom P M (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m) = M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) m :=
  descGerm_germAt P.ideal_fg M (M.value P) (selfHom P M)
    (fun {_ _} f m => selfHom_restriction P M f m) X m

/-- The germ at the terminal object, which inverts `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitSelfHom`. -/
def colimitSelfInv (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    M.value P ⟶ (colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg).obj M :=
  germ P.ideal_fg M (self P)

/-- `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitSelfInv` sends `m` to its germ at the terminal object. -/
theorem colimitSelfInv_apply (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u}) (m : M.value P) :
    colimitSelfInv P M m = germAt P.ideal_fg M (self P) m := rfl

/-- **The colimit of step 2 at a presented pair is the value of the pair-module there.** The
index category has a terminal object, so the filtered colimit is computed at it. This is what
makes the construction of this file an *extension* of
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum`: at a presented pair it gives back
`Stacks.PairSite.sectionsComplex`, where conditions (c) and (d) are known. -/
def colimitSelfIso (P : Pair.{u}) (M : PairModule.{u}) :
    (colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg).obj M ≅ M.value P where
  hom := colimitSelfHom P M
  inv := colimitSelfInv P M
  hom_inv_id := by
    refine hom_ext_germAt P.ideal_fg fun X m => ?_
    have h1 : colimitSelfHom P M (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m) =
        M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) m := colimitSelfHom_germAt P M X m
    have h2 : colimitSelfInv P M (M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) m) =
        germAt P.ideal_fg M X m := germAt_restriction P.ideal_fg M (toSelf X) m
    change colimitSelfInv P M (colimitSelfHom P M (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m)) =
      germAt P.ideal_fg M X m
    rw [h1, h2]
  inv_hom_id := by
    refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun m => ?_)
    have h1 : colimitSelfHom P M (colimitSelfInv P M m) =
        M.restriction (Hom.toHom (toSelf (self P))) m :=
      colimitSelfHom_germAt P M (self P) m
    change colimitSelfHom P M (colimitSelfInv P M m) = m
    rw [h1]
    exact PairModule.restriction_id_apply M P m

/-- The comparison map from the colimit at a presented pair is natural in the pair-module. -/
theorem colimitSelfHom_naturality (P : Pair.{u}) {M N : PairModule.{u}} (α : M ⟶ N) :
    (colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg).map α ≫ colimitSelfHom P N =
      colimitSelfHom P M ≫ PresheafOfModules.Hom.app α P.ix := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt P.ideal_fg fun X m => ?_
  change colimitSelfHom P N ((colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg).map α (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m)) =
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app α P.ix (colimitSelfHom P M (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m))
  rw [colimitSelfHom_germAt]
  erw [germAt_naturality, colimitSelfHom_germAt]
  exact (PairModule.naturality_apply α (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) m).symm

/-- **The colimit functor of a presented pair is evaluation at that pair.** -/
def colimitSelfNatIso (P : Pair.{u}) :
    colimitFunctor P.ideal_fg ≅ PairModule.evaluation P :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (colimitSelfIso P) (fun α => colimitSelfHom_naturality P α)

/-- **The colimit complex at a presented pair is the complex of sections there.** -/
def colimitComplexSelfIso (P : Pair.{u}) (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ) :
    (colimitComplexFunctor P.ideal_fg).obj K ≅ sectionsComplex K P :=
  haveI : (PairModule.evaluation P).Additive :=
    inferInstanceAs (PresheafOfModules.evaluation structureRings.{u} P.ix).Additive
  (NatIso.mapHomologicalComplex (colimitSelfNatIso P) (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).app K

/-! ### The complex level -/

/-- **Datum (3) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit**, on a complex of pair-modules: a map of
complexes of `A`-modules `K(A, I) ⟶ K(B, IB)`. Its commutation with the differentials is the
naturality of `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap`. -/
def colimitComplexMap (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ) :
    (colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj K ⟶
      (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj ((colimitComplexFunctor hJ).obj K) where
  f n := colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ (K.X n)
  comm' n m _ := (colimitMap_naturality φ hI hJ hφ (K.d n m)).symm

/-- In degree `n`, `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap` is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap` on the `n`-th term. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitComplexMap_f (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ) (n : ℤ) :
    (colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ K).f n = colimitMap φ hI hJ hφ (K.X n) := rfl

/-- The comparison map of complexes is natural in the complex of pair-modules. -/
theorem colimitComplexMap_naturality (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) {K K' : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ} (a : K ⟶ K') :
    colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ K ≫
        (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map ((colimitComplexFunctor hJ).map a) =
      (colimitComplexFunctor hI).map a ≫ colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ K' :=
  HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n =>
    (colimitMap_naturality φ hI hJ hφ (a.f n)).symm

/-- **`colim 𝒪[0] ≅ A[0]`**: the identification `colim 𝒪 ≅ A` read on the complex concentrated
in degree zero, which is where the augmentation of the tag lands. -/
def colimitStructureSingleIso (hI : I.FG) :
    (colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj structureSingle.{u} ≅
      (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A) :=
  (HomologicalComplex.singleMapHomologicalComplex
      (colimitFunctor hI) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).app structureModule.{u} ≪≫
    (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).mapIso (colimitStructureIso hI)

/-- **Datum (2) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit**: the augmentation `K(A, I) ⟶ A[0]`
obtained from an augmentation `𝒦• ⟶ 𝒪[0]` of a complex of pair-modules. -/
def colimitAugmentation (hI : I.FG) {K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ}
    (α : K ⟶ structureSingle.{u}) :
    (colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj K ⟶
      (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A) :=
  (colimitComplexFunctor hI).map α ≫ (colimitStructureSingleIso hI).hom

/-- The augmentation at the colimit is the colimit of `α` followed by `colim 𝒪[0] ≅ A[0]`. -/
theorem colimitAugmentation_eq (hI : I.FG) {K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ}
    (α : K ⟶ structureSingle.{u}) :
    colimitAugmentation hI α =
      (colimitComplexFunctor hI).map α ≫ (colimitStructureSingleIso hI).hom := rfl

/-- The identification `colim 𝒪[0] ≅ A[0]` is compatible with the comparison maps of datum
(3): this is the degreewise content of condition (a). -/
theorem colimitStructureSingleIso_naturality (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) :
    colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ structureSingle.{u} ≫
        (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map (colimitStructureSingleIso hJ).hom =
      (colimitStructureSingleIso hI).hom ≫ LocalCohomology.singleRingHom φ := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n => ?_
  by_cases h : n = 0
  · subst h
    exact colimitMap_structureModule φ hI hJ hφ
  · exact (Functor.map_isZero (ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ)
      (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0
        (ModuleCat.of B B) n h)).eq_of_tgt _ _

/-- **Condition (a) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit, on the nose.** The comparison maps of
datum (3) are compatible with the augmentations of datum (2), in the shape
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.map_augmentation` demands. -/
theorem colimitComplexMap_augmentation (φ : A →+* B) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) {K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ}
    (α : K ⟶ structureSingle.{u}) :
    colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ K ≫
        (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map (colimitAugmentation hJ α) =
      colimitAugmentation hI α ≫ LocalCohomology.singleRingHom φ := by
  rw [colimitAugmentation_eq, colimitAugmentation_eq, Functor.map_comp, ← Category.assoc,
    colimitComplexMap_naturality, Category.assoc, colimitStructureSingleIso_naturality,
    Category.assoc]

/-- **Condition (b) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] at the colimit, on the nose.** The comparison maps of
datum (3) compose, in the shape `Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.map_map` demands. No
homotopy and no quasi-isomorphism intervenes: the composition law of
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport` is an equality of functors by `rfl`. -/
theorem colimitComplexMap_comp (φ : A →+* B) (ψ : B →+* D) (hI : I.FG) (hJ : J.FG) (hL : L.FG)
    (hφ : J = Ideal.map φ I) (hψ : L = Ideal.map ψ J) (hχ : L = Ideal.map (ψ.comp φ) I)
    (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ) :
    colimitComplexMap (ψ.comp φ) hI hL hχ K =
      colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ K ≫
        (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map (colimitComplexMap ψ hJ hL hψ K) ≫
          (LocalCohomology.restrictScalarsCompComplexIso φ ψ).hom.app
            ((colimitComplexFunctor hL).obj K) :=
  HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n =>
    colimitMap_comp φ ψ hI hJ hL hφ hψ hχ (K.X n)

/-! ### Exactness of the colimit, and quasi-isomorphisms -/

/-- **AB5 at the shape of the index category.** The colimits of `A`-modules indexed by the index
category of step 2 are exact. This is Mathlib's `AB5 (ModuleCat A)` read at the shape
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver A I`, which is small and, by
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isFiltered`, filtered. It is the input the commutation of homology
with the colimit (`Stacks.HomologyColimit.preservesColimitsOfShape_homologyFunctor`) needs. -/
theorem hasExactColimitsOfShape (hI : I.FG) :
    HasExactColimitsOfShape (PairOver A I) (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  inferInstance

/-- **Quasi-isomorphisms are stable under the colimit of step 2.** The colimits of `A`-modules at
this shape are exact, so homology commutes with them and a colimit of quasi-isomorphisms is a
quasi-isomorphism. -/
theorem isStableUnderColimitsOfShape_quasiIso (hI : I.FG) :
    (HomologicalComplex.quasiIso (ModuleCat.{u} A)
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).IsStableUnderColimitsOfShape (PairOver A I) :=
  have := hasExactColimitsOfShape (I := I) hI
  Stacks.HomologyColimit.isStableUnderColimitsOfShape_quasiIso (ComplexShape.up ℤ)

/-- **A colimit of quasi-isomorphisms over the index category is a quasi-isomorphism**, for
arbitrary colimit cocones. This is the form the colimit of step 2 is used in: the cocone
produced by `PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor` is not the one the colimit API chooses. -/
theorem quasiIso_of_isColimit (hI : I.FG)
    {F G : PairOver A I ⥤ CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ} {cF : Cocone F} {cG : Cocone G}
    (hF : IsColimit cF) (hG : IsColimit cG) (α : F ⟶ G) (hα : ∀ X, QuasiIso (α.app X))
    (φ : cF.pt ⟶ cG.pt) (hφ : ∀ X, cF.ι.app X ≫ φ = α.app X ≫ cG.ι.app X) :
    QuasiIso φ :=
  (isStableUnderColimitsOfShape_quasiIso (I := I) hI).condition F G cF cG hF hG α
    (fun X => hα X) φ hφ

/-- **A colimit of quasi-isomorphisms over the index category is a quasi-isomorphism**, for the
colimits the colimit API chooses. -/
theorem quasiIso_colimMap (hI : I.FG)
    {F G : PairOver A I ⥤ CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ} (α : F ⟶ G)
    (hα : ∀ X, QuasiIso (α.app X)) : QuasiIso (colimMap α) :=
  quasiIso_of_isColimit hI (colimit.isColimit F) (colimit.isColimit G) α hα _
    (fun X => (colimit.ι_map α X).symm ▸ rfl)

/-! ### Presenting a prescribed generating family -/

/-- **An object of the index category whose ideal is generated by lifts of a prescribed finite
family.** If `f₁, …, f_r` generate `I`, there is an object `X` of the index category whose
structure map is injective, together with elements `g₁, …, g_r` of `X.pair.ring` mapping to the
`f i` and generating the ideal of `X.pair`.

The construction is `Stacks.PairSite.Pair.ofEval` applied to `f` itself with the *variables* as
the chosen polynomials: the ring is `ℤ[x₁, …, x_r]` modulo the relations the `f i` satisfy in
`A`, so it injects into `A` with image `ℤ[f₁, …, f_r]`, and its ideal is by construction the
span of the classes of the variables.

This strengthens `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_approx_eq`, which produces an object
realising a prescribed approximation but with whatever finite generating family
`Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox.exists_fin_span` returns. Recognising the colimit of step 2
as the Čech complex on `f` needs the generating family upstairs to be a lift of `f`. -/
theorem exists_pairOver_lift_span {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) :
    ∃ (X : PairOver A I) (g : Fin r → X.pair.ring),
      (∀ i, X.hom (g i) = f i) ∧ Ideal.span (Set.range g) = X.pair.ideal ∧
        Function.Injective X.hom := by
  have hmap : Ideal.map (Pair.ofEvalHom f)
      (Pair.ofEval f (fun j : Fin r => MvPolynomial.X j)).ideal = I := by
    rw [Pair.map_ideal_ofEvalHom,
      show (fun j : Fin r => Pair.eval f (MvPolynomial.X j)) = f from funext (Pair.eval_X f)]
    exact hf
  refine ⟨⟨Pair.ofEval f (fun j : Fin r => MvPolynomial.X j), Pair.ofEvalHom f, hmap⟩,
    fun j => Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval f)) (MvPolynomial.X j), Pair.eval_X f,
    ?_, Pair.ofEvalHom_injective f⟩
  change Ideal.span (Set.range fun j : Fin r =>
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval f)) (MvPolynomial.X j)) =
    (Ideal.span (Set.range fun j : Fin r => (MvPolynomial.X j : presentationRing.{u} r))).map
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval f)))
  rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-! ### The colimit datum at a presented pair

At a presented pair `P` the index category has a terminal object, so
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexSelfIso` identifies the colimit complex with the complex
of sections. The lemmas below say that this identification carries the datum of
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum` onto the colimit datum: the comparison maps of datum (3),
the identification `colim 𝒪 ≅ A`, and the augmentation of datum (2) all correspond. -/

/-- **The identification `colim 𝒪 ≅ A` at a presented pair is restriction to the terminal
object.** Both maps send the germ of `r ∈ A₀` at `X` to the image of `r` under the structure map
of `X`. -/
theorem colimitStructureHom_eq_colimitSelfHom (P : Pair.{u}) :
    colimitStructureHom P.ideal_fg = colimitSelfHom P structureModule.{u} := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt P.ideal_fg fun X r => ?_
  exact (colimitStructureHom_germAt P.ideal_fg X r).trans
    ((structureModule_restriction_apply (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) r).symm.trans
      (colimitSelfHom_germAt P structureModule.{u} X r).symm)

/-- **Datum (3) at the colimit of a presented pair is the restriction map of the pair-module.**
The comparison `colim_{(A₀,I₀)} M ⟶ colim_{(B₀,J₀)} M` attached to a morphism of pairs
`f : P ⟶ Q` becomes, under the identifications at the two terminal objects, the restriction map
`M(P) ⟶ M(Q)`. The proof is the identity `toSelf ((transport f).obj X) = toSelf X ≫ f` of
morphisms of pairs, which holds because a morphism of pairs is determined by its ring map. -/
theorem colimitMap_self (M : PairModule.{u}) {P Q : Pair.{u}} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    colimitMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal M ≫
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars f.toRingHom).map (colimitSelfHom Q M) =
      colimitSelfHom P M ≫ M.restriction f := by
  refine hom_ext_germAt P.ideal_fg fun X m => ?_
  have hkey : Hom.toHom (toSelf ((transport f.toRingHom f.map_ideal).obj X)) =
      Hom.toHom (toSelf X) ≫ f := Pair.Hom.ext' rfl
  change colimitSelfHom Q M (colimitMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal M
      (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m)) =
    M.restriction f (colimitSelfHom P M (germAt P.ideal_fg M X m))
  rw [colimitSelfHom_germAt, colimitMap_germAt]
  erw [colimitSelfHom_germAt, hkey]
  exact PairModule.restriction_comp_apply M (Hom.toHom (toSelf X)) f m

/-- In degree `n`, the forward map of `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexSelfIso` is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitSelfHom` on the `n`-th term. -/
@[simp]
theorem colimitComplexSelfIso_hom_f (P : Pair.{u}) (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ)
    (n : ℤ) : (colimitComplexSelfIso P K).hom.f n = colimitSelfHom P (K.X n) := rfl

/-- **Datum (3) at the colimit of a presented pair is `Stacks.PairSite.sectionsMap`.** The
complex-level form of `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitMap_self`. -/
theorem colimitComplexMap_self (K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ) {P Q : Pair.{u}}
    (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    colimitComplexMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal K ≫
        (CochainComplex.restrictScalars f.toRingHom).map (colimitComplexSelfIso Q K).hom =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P K).hom ≫ sectionsMap K f :=
  HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n => colimitMap_self (K.X n) f

/-- **`colim 𝒪[0] ≅ A[0]` at a presented pair factors through the sections of `𝒪[0]`.** Only
degree zero has content, and there it is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitStructureHom_eq_colimitSelfHom`. -/
theorem colimitStructureSingleIso_self (P : Pair.{u}) :
    (colimitStructureSingleIso P.ideal_fg).hom =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P structureSingle.{u}).hom ≫
        (sectionsStructureSingleIso P).hom := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n => ?_
  by_cases h : n = 0
  · subst h
    exact colimitStructureHom_eq_colimitSelfHom P
  · exact (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0
      (ModuleCat.of P.ring P.ring) n h).eq_of_tgt _ _

/-- **Datum (2) at the colimit of a presented pair is `Stacks.PairSite.sectionsAugmentation`.**
This is the transport of the augmentation that identifying the colimit complex at a presented
pair with the complex of sections requires. -/
theorem colimitAugmentation_self (P : Pair.{u}) {K : CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ}
    (α : K ⟶ structureSingle.{u}) :
    colimitAugmentation P.ideal_fg α =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P K).hom ≫ sectionsAugmentation α P := by
  have : (PairModule.evaluation P).Additive :=
    inferInstanceAs (PresheafOfModules.evaluation structureRings.{u} P.ix).Additive
  have hnat : (colimitComplexFunctor P.ideal_fg).map α ≫
        (colimitComplexSelfIso P structureSingle.{u}).hom =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P K).hom ≫
        (StrictReplacement.sectionsFunctor structureRings.{u} P.ix).map α :=
    (NatIso.mapHomologicalComplex (colimitSelfNatIso P) (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).hom.naturality α
  rw [colimitAugmentation_eq, colimitStructureSingleIso_self, sectionsAugmentation_eq,
    ← Category.assoc, hnat]
  exact Category.assoc _ _ _

end PairOver

/-! ### Conditions (c) and (d) at the presented pairs -/

open PairOver

/-- **Condition (c) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for the colimit complex, at a morphism of presented
pairs.** For `f : P ⟶ Q` in the category of pairs the comparison
`K(P.ring, P.ideal) ⊗^L_{P.ring} Q.ring ⟶ K(Q.ring, Q.ideal)` built from the colimit is an
isomorphism in `D(Q.ring)`.

Under `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_self` the comparison map of the colimit datum
differs from `Stacks.PairSite.sectionsMap` only by the two isomorphisms at the terminal objects,
and `Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_left` /
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_right` turn those into isomorphisms of the
comparison. So this is the datum's own field
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum.isIso_derivedBaseChange`, transported.

This is **not** `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitBaseChange`, which quantifies over every ring map
`A →+* B` with `I.FG`, not only over morphisms of presented pairs. -/
theorem isIso_derivedBaseChange_colimitComplexMap_self (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u})
    {P Q : Pair.{u}} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    IsIso (LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange f.toRingHom
      (colimitComplexMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal Dat.complex)) := by
  have hsq : colimitComplexMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal Dat.complex ≫
      ((CochainComplex.restrictScalars f.toRingHom).mapIso
        (colimitComplexSelfIso Q Dat.complex)).hom =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex).hom ≫ sectionsMap Dat.complex f :=
    colimitComplexMap_self Dat.complex f
  have hdec : colimitComplexMap f.toRingHom P.ideal_fg Q.ideal_fg f.map_ideal Dat.complex =
      (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex).hom ≫
        (sectionsMap Dat.complex f ≫
          (CochainComplex.restrictScalars f.toRingHom).map
            (colimitComplexSelfIso Q Dat.complex).inv) :=
    ((Iso.eq_comp_inv _).mpr hsq).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)
  rw [hdec, LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_left,
    LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_right]
  have := Dat.isIso_derivedBaseChange f
  infer_instance

/-- **Condition (d) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for the colimit complex, at a presented pair.** For a
finite family generating the ideal of a presented pair `P` there is an isomorphism in
`D(P.ring)` from the extended alternating Čech complex on that family to the colimit complex,
carrying the augmentation of the former onto that of the latter.

This is the datum's own field `Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum.exists_cech_iso` composed with
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexSelfIso`, the augmentations matching by
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitAugmentation_self`.

This is **not** `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitCechIso`, which quantifies over every ring `A` with a
finitely generated ideal, not only over the presented pairs. -/
theorem exists_cech_iso_colimit_self (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) (P : Pair.{u}) {r : ℕ}
    (g : Fin r → P.ring) (hg : Ideal.span (Set.range g) = P.ideal) :
    ∃ e : LocalCohomology.extendedCechObject g (ModuleCat.of P.ring P.ring) ≅
        DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((colimitComplexFunctor P.ideal_fg).obj Dat.complex),
      e.hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map (colimitAugmentation P.ideal_fg Dat.augmentation) ≫
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} P.ring) 0).app
            (ModuleCat.of P.ring P.ring)).inv =
        LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentationHom g (ModuleCat.of P.ring P.ring) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := Dat.exists_cech_iso P g hg
  refine ⟨e ≪≫ (DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex)).symm, ?_⟩
  have key : DerivedCategory.Q.map (colimitAugmentation P.ideal_fg Dat.augmentation) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex).hom ≫
        DerivedCategory.Q.map (sectionsAugmentation Dat.augmentation P) := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, colimitAugmentation_self]
  have hid : ∀ {Z : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} P.ring)}
      (t : DerivedCategory.Q.obj (sectionsComplex Dat.complex P) ⟶ Z),
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex).inv ≫
        DerivedCategory.Q.map (colimitComplexSelfIso P Dat.complex).hom ≫ t = t := by
    intro Z t
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp, Iso.inv_hom_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id,
      Category.id_comp]
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, Functor.mapIso_inv, key, Category.assoc, hid]
  exact he

/-! ### The assembly -/

/-- **Condition (c) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for the colimit complex of a datum on presented
pairs**: for every ring map `φ : A →+* B` and `J = IB`, the induced map
`K(A, I) ⊗^L_A B ⟶ K(B, J)` is an isomorphism in `D(B)`.

This is exactly the field `Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.isIso_derivedBaseChange`
for the complex `(PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex`. It is not proved in this
file: it is a statement in a derived category, and carrying it across the filtered colimit needs
the exactness of filtered colimits of `A`-modules at the shape `PairOver A I` and the stability
of quasi-isomorphisms under filtered colimits. It holds for every datum, by
`Stacks.PairSite.colimitBaseChange`. -/
def ColimitBaseChange (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) : Prop :=
  ∀ {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B) (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    (J : Ideal B) (hJ : J.FG) (hφ : J = I.map φ),
    IsIso (LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange φ
      (PairOver.colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ Dat.complex))

/-- **Condition (d) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for the colimit complex of a datum on presented
pairs**: for a finite family generating `I` there is an isomorphism in `D(A)` from the extended
alternating Čech complex on that family to `K(A, I)`, compatibly with the augmentations.

This is exactly the field `Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.exists_cech_iso` for the
complex `(PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex`. Like
`Stacks.PairSite.ColimitBaseChange` it is not proved here, and like it holds for every datum, by
`Stacks.PairSite.colimitCechIso`. -/
def ColimitCechIso (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) : Prop :=
  ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    (_ : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I),
    ∃ e : LocalCohomology.extendedCechObject f (ModuleCat.of A A) ≅
        DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex),
      e.hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map (PairOver.colimitAugmentation hI Dat.augmentation) ≫
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).app
            (ModuleCat.of A A)).inv =
        LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentationHom f (ModuleCat.of A A)

/-- **The functorial Čech datum built from a datum on presented pairs by the filtered colimit of
step 2 of [Stacks, Tag 099D].** Data (1), (2) and (3) are
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor`,
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitAugmentation` and
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap`; conditions (a) and (b) are
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_augmentation` and
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexMap_comp`, both on the nose. -/
def colimitCechData (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) (hc : ColimitBaseChange Dat)
    (hd : ColimitCechIso Dat) : LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.{u} where
  complex _ _ _ hI := (PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex
  augmentation _ _ _ hI := PairOver.colimitAugmentation hI Dat.augmentation
  map φ _ hI _ hJ hφ := PairOver.colimitComplexMap φ hI hJ hφ Dat.complex
  map_augmentation φ _ hI _ hJ hφ :=
    PairOver.colimitComplexMap_augmentation φ hI hJ hφ Dat.augmentation
  map_map φ ψ _ hI _ hJ _ hK hφ hψ :=
    PairOver.colimitComplexMap_comp φ ψ hI hJ hK hφ hψ _ Dat.complex
  isIso_derivedBaseChange φ I hI J hJ hφ := hc φ I hI J hJ hφ
  exists_cech_iso A _ _ f I hI hf := hd A f I hI hf

/-- **Step 2 of [Stacks, Tag 099D]**: a Čech datum on the category of presented pairs whose
colimit complex satisfies conditions (c) and (d) gives a functorial Čech datum for *all* pairs
`(A, I)` with `I` finitely generated.

No `@[stacks 099D]` attribute is attached: the tag asks for an unconditional
`Nonempty Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData`, and this statement takes three inputs.
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData` is it with the two conditions discharged, and
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_functorialCechData` — which carries the attribute — is that fed
the datum `Stacks.PairSite.exists_presentedCechDatum`. -/
theorem exists_functorialCechData_of_presented (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u})
    (hc : ColimitBaseChange Dat) (hd : ColimitCechIso Dat) :
    Nonempty LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.{u} :=
  ⟨colimitCechData Dat hc hd⟩

end Stacks.PairSite

end
